--
--  demo\theGUI\hMenu.exw
--  =====================
--
--  NOTE: It is seriously impractical to extract all the code in theGUI.e that deals with the
--        focus and alt-tab aspects of menu handling, see (eg) the comment above the forward
--        definition of tg_ensure_popup() should you need proof. What I have done is allow
--        just 1 of the 47 routines (not counting changes to the core WndProc and equivalent
--        GTK scatterings) needed to deal with menus, being the draw_menu, via an otherwise 
--        undocumented gSetGlobal("drawmenu"), with no option to override size or position.
--        Therefore, as-is, this is only concerned with / demonstrates custom drawing.
--
--        You could of course factor out other code fragments in a similar fashion, but my 
--        strongest advice would be to leave all the inter-routine linkage stuff well alone.
--         [One of these days I'm going to write meself one of those call graph doobries.]
--        For instance you might want to change mousemove to something which determines if
--        the mouse is on the icon/text/keyboard shortcut, factoring out the when and why
--        they should be called is one thing, but the actual calls to tg_hide_submenus()
--        and tg_open_child_menu() should remain in theGUI/tg_menu_mousemove(), iyswim,
--        aka if moving a call here causes insurmountable issues then don't move it here.
--
--        Should you be interested in how it works, see win_menus.exw, gtk_menus.exw, and
--        pwa\js\poc\menus.html for the absolute bare minimum code required.
--
--       toggle checked and radio menu items, w/o closing the menu. [DONE!]
--
-- TODO: menubar hover/keyboard stuff [close done]
--       (here) new/open/close update recent items
--       empty submenus should be auto-disabled [now initially good, check again when update_recent_menu() done]
--       hovering on the menubar is using "previous hover open" when it should be using "any".
--
